' Shared redraw/caching logic for the SceneGraph shape components under
' `components/Shapes/` (RoundedRectangle, Circle, Triangle, Polygon). Each
' component owns exactly one private BGE.Renderer over its own roBitmap and
' renders into a `tmp:/`-cached PNG, the same Poster-extends/Finish()+GetPng()+
' tmp:/-file pattern proven by the QR-code SceneGraph library referenced in
' specs/2026-08-24-scenegraph-shape-components-design.md.
'
' A SceneGraph component's own compile scope only includes files reachable via
' `import` (unlike the flat "source" scope a plain BrighterScript app gets for
' free) - and BrighterScript type-checks a whole imported class/file, not just
' the members actually called, so importing BGE.Renderer here pulls in its full
' transitive dependency graph. Every shape component imports only this one file
' to get the whole engine in scope, rather than repeating this list four times.
' Paths are relative (not `pkg:/`-absolute) so they resolve correctly however
' a consumer's own bsconfig `files` remapping relocates this whole `source/`
' tree (e.g. `examples/*` copies it under `source/roku_modules/source/`, ropm
' installs it under `source/roku_modules/<pkg>/`) - relative paths between
' sibling engine files stay correct under any uniform prefix like that.
import "../engine/renderer/Renderer.bs"
import "../engine/Canvas.bs"
import "../engine/colliders/CircleCollider.bs"
import "../engine/colliders/Collider.bs"
import "../engine/colliders/RectangleCollider.bs"
